#: ../../../policy/CMP0230.rst:2
msgid "CMP0230"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0230.rst:6
msgid ""
":module:`CMakeAddFortranSubdirectory` builds the MinGW project with the "
"parent configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0230.rst:9
msgid ""
"When the parent project uses MSVC without a Fortran compiler, "
"the :command:`cmake_add_fortran_subdirectory` command builds the Fortran "
"project as an external project using a MinGW ``gfortran`` and a single-"
"config :generator:`MinGW Makefiles` generator.  CMake 4.5 and below "
"configure that project without :variable:`CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`, so it is built "
"without configuration-specific flags regardless of the "
"parent's :variable:`CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE` or the configuration selected in a "
"multi-config generator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0230.rst:18
msgid ""
"CMake 4.6 and above prefer to set :variable:`CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE` in the MinGW "
"project to the configuration being built by the parent project. With a multi-"
"config parent, the MinGW build tree is shared by all configurations, so it "
"is reconfigured when the configuration being built differs from the one it "
"was last configured with.  A :variable:`CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE` given in the "
"``CMAKE_COMMAND_LINE`` option is overridden."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0230.rst:26
msgid ""
"The ``OLD`` behavior for this policy is to configure the MinGW project "
"without setting :variable:`CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`.  The ``NEW`` behavior is to "
"set :variable:`CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE` to the parent project's configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0230.rst:30
msgid ""
"This policy is checked when :command:`cmake_add_fortran_subdirectory` is "
"called.  It has no effect when the Fortran project is added directly "
"with :command:`add_subdirectory`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/include/STANDARD_ADVICE.rst:1
msgid ""
"This policy was introduced in CMake version |INTRODUCED_IN_CMAKE_VERSION|. "
"It may be set by :command:`cmake_policy` "
"or :command:`cmake_minimum_required`. If it is not set, CMake |"
"WARNS_OR_DOES_NOT_WARN|, and uses ``OLD`` behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/include/DEPRECATED.rst:2
msgid ""
"The ``OLD`` behavior of a policy is :ref:`deprecated by definition <cmake-"
"policies-intro>` and may be removed in a future version of CMake."
msgstr ""
